  "content": {
    "id": "p9-q10-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "10",
    "prompt": "Four dice are rolled and the product of the numbers is recorded. Find the probability that the result is a multiple of 3.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\dfrac{65}{81}$",
      "worked": "Let $A$ be the event that the product is a multiple of 3. Its complement occurs when none of the dice shows 3 or 6. Each die then has four suitable outcomes: 1, 2, 4 and 5. The rolls are independent.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Pr(A')&=\\left(\\frac{4}{6}\\right)^4\\\\\\Pr(A')&=\\frac{16}{81}\\end{align*}$$\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Pr(A)&=1-\\Pr(A')\\\\\\Pr(A)&=1-\\frac{16}{81}\\\\\\Pr(A)&=\\frac{65}{81}\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 38
  },
